<title>USA: Brooks Fiber expands AT&amp;T relationship.</title>
<headline>Brooks Fiber expands AT&amp;T relationship.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brooks Fiber Properties Inc said Thursday it will expand its relationship with AT&amp;T Corp as it moves further into the switched access business.</p>
<p>AT&amp;T is expected to use Brooks Fiber networks for origination and termination of its long-distance customer calls. The move will allow AT&amp;T to bypass incumbent local exchange carriers, Brooks Fiber said.</p>
<p>Financial terms were not announced.</p>
<p>Brooks Fiber provides local telecommunications services in 36 U.S. cities.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
